    "incident_title": "Orders stuck in \"Processing\", confirmation emails not sent",
    "outcome": "inconclusive",
    "summary": "Orders stuck in \"Processing\" and missing confirmation emails are best explained by orders-worker-7 crash-looping (exit code 1) since about 13:17-13:20. Because orders-worker-N is statically bound to Kafka partition N and there is no dead-letter queue, partition 7 of order-events has stopped being consumed; consumer lag on partition 7 rises steadily to about 505 by 14:05. Orders on that partition never reach orders-db or notification-svc, which explains the stuck orders and missing emails. The checkout-svc v4.1.0 deploy at 13:05 is the leading suspect for the poison message, but I could not confirm the crash cause: logging-es timed out on every log query. The Kafka broker-2 restart at 13:28 does not explain the onset, since the partition 7 lag and the first worker-7 crash both precede it. A second pod, orders-worker-2, began crash-looping at about 13:52, and its cause is also unconfirmed. No alert fired for consumer lag or crash-looping; the only alert was the Kafka under-replicated partitions warning.",
